	//    - Then the smallest valid k is k_min = k0 + m_min * p, where m_min = max(0, ceil((lower_bound - k0) / p)).
	//      But since k0 < p and lower_bound is 0 or 1, and p >= 2:
	//      If r >= 1: lower_bound = 0. k0 >= 0, so k0 >= 0 always. So m_min = 0, k_min = k0.
